What are Ultrasonic Cutters?
Ultrasonic cutters are precision cutting tools that utilize high-frequency vibrations (typically above 20 kHz) to slice through materials with minimal friction and heat generation. These devices employ a blade or horn that oscillates at ultrasonic frequencies, enabling clean cuts in diverse materials ranging from soft textiles to rigid plastics and composites. The technology delivers sealed edges without fraying, melting, or material deformation, making it ideal for sensitive applications where traditional mechanical or thermal methods fall short.
